# text = After a few minutes of entire silence between them , John Knightley began with replied Emma said Mr . John Knightley presently , with some slyness she replied with a smile of astonishment and she walked on , amusing herself in the consideration of the blunders which often arise from a partial knowledge of circumstances , of the mistakes which people of high pretensions to judgment are for ever falling into ; and not very well pleased with her brother for imagining her blind and ignorant , and in want of counsel .
