# text = Time , she knew , must be allowed for this being thoroughly done ; and she could suppose herself but an indifferent judge of such matters in general , and very inadequate to sympathise in an attachment to Mr . Elton in particular ; but it seemed to her reasonable that at Harriet's age , and with the entire extinction of all hope , such a progress might be made towards a state of composure by the time of Mr . Elton's return , as to allow them all to meet again in the common routine of acquaintance , without any danger of betraying sentiments or increasing them .
