# text = Mrs . and Miss Bates occupied the drawing-room floor ; and there , in the very moderate-sized apartment , which was every thing to them , the visitors were most cordially and even gratefully welcomed ; the quiet neat old lady , who with her knitting was seated in the warmest corner , wanting even to give up her place to Miss Woodhouse , and her more active , talking daughter , almost ready to overpower them with care and kindness , thanks for their visit , solicitude for their shoes , anxious inquiries after Mr . Woodhouse's health , cheerful communications about her mother's , and sweet-cake from the beaufet
