# text = She had not been prepared to have Jane Fairfax succeed Mr . Elton ; but he was actually hurried off by Miss Bates , she jumped away from him at last abruptly to the Coles , to usher in a letter from her niece Emma's politeness was at hand directly , to say , with smiling interest replied the happily deceived aunt , while eagerly hunting for the letter All this spoken extremely fast obliged Miss Bates to stop for breath ; and Emma said something very civil about the excellence of Miss Fairfax's handwriting replied Miss Bates , highly gratified addressing her And Emma had the advantage of hearing her own silly compliment repeated twice over before the good old lady could comprehend it .
