# text = The party did not break up without Emma's being positively secured for the two first dances by the hero of the evening , nor without her overhearing Mr . Weston whisper to his wife One thing only was wanting to make the prospect of the ball completely satisfactory to Emma -- its being fixed for a day within the granted term of Frank Churchill's stay in Surry ; for , in spite of Mr . Weston's confidence , she could not think it so very impossible that the Churchills might not allow their nephew to remain a day beyond his fortnight .
