# text = The dread of being awakened from the happiest dream , was perhaps the most prominent feeling he soon resumed ; and in a tone of such sincere , decided , intelligible tenderness as was tolerably convincing While he spoke , Emma's mind was most busy , and , with all the wonderful velocity of thought , had been able -- and yet without losing a word -- to catch and comprehend the exact truth of the whole ; to see that Harriet's hopes had been entirely groundless , a mistake , a delusion , as complete a delusion as any of her own -- that Harriet was nothing ; that she was every thing herself ; that what she had been saying relative to Harriet had been all taken as the language of her own feelings ; and that her agitation , her doubts , her reluctance , her discouragement , had been all received as discouragement from herself .--
